    "## SALES PERFORMANCE AND REVENUE ANALYSIS"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ab91eef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📌Project Overview"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2a776d0d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This project is a part of business intelligence case study designed to analyse company sales performance, customer behaviour, product trends, and operational insights. It demonstrates advanced use of BI tools such as **Microsoft Excel, Power BI, DAX, and SQL** to build a board room ready dashboard.\n",
    "The report is structured into multiple pages, each focusing on a different aspect of sales performance, with visuals optimized for storytelling and executive decision making.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5cb43fe9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🏢 Company Context \n",
    "**Client Name:** Samudra Marine Supplies Pvt Ltd\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "The Company is a Thane-based distributor of **Marine products**, including chemicals, water treatment solutions, fuel oil, mooring ropes, and maintenance supplies. Through its strong global supply network, the company serves a wide range of customer segments such as ship owners, managers, chandlers, and offshore operators across India & subcontinent.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Company set a strategic goal of reaching ₹50 Million in revenue by 2025. However, it lacked centralized Business Intelligence(BI) system to effectively monitor performance and support data-driven decision-making.\n",
    "Recent performance data(2020-2025) indicated a decline in sales after 2023, with year-on-year growth turning negative in 2025, raising concerns about business sustainability and growth momentum.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0a81b892",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🎯 Project Objective\n",
    "The objective of this project is to analyze historical sales and revenue data to:\n",
    "- Identify key trends and inflection point where growth began to decline\n",
    "- Highlight performance gaps against ₹50M target\n",
    "- Diagnose the root causes of revenue drop across customers, products, and regions\n",
    "- Uncover key business risks and inefficiencies affecting profitability\n",
    "- Provide data-driven insights and recommendations to support strategic decision-making"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32337c5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🛠️ Tools & Technologies\n",
    "- ERP- Source Data\n",
    "- Excel- Extract source data \n",
    "- Excel Power Query – Data cleaning and transformation.\n",
    "- Python - to Load data into PostgreSQL\n",
    "- PostgreSQL - creating measures and views\n",
    "- DAX – Custom measures and calculations.\n",
    "- Power BI Desktop – Data modeling, visualization, and report building.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e441cf68",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data Preparation & Confidentiality\n",
    "\n",
    "- Imported data in Excel from the database\n",
    "- Cleaned,prepared data in excel power query\n",
    "- Analysed data and Created views in PostgreSQL\n",
    "- Loaded data and SQL views in Power BI\n",
    "- Constructed a snowflake schema tailored for the data model\n",
    "- Built interactive dashboards with clear KPIs.\n",
    "- Applied DAX measures and calculations for advanced analytics\n",
    "- Delivered insights into sales, profit, customers, products etc.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "-\tOriginal dataset contained customer, vessel, port, product, and order details in a single table.\n",
    "-\tSeparated into normalized 11 tables (Orders, Customers, Customers Segment, Vessels, Products, Product Category, Ports, Port Zone, Sales Region, Sales Representative, Country Code) and saved in CSV file to load tables in PostgreSQL\n",
    "-\tAnonymized sensitive fields (names, codes) while preserving structure and relationships.\n",
    "-\tEnsured confidentiality without losing analytical value\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6dd5343d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    " ### Loading into PostgreSQL\n",
    "-\tEach table created in excel saved as separate CSV files \n",
    "-\tPython script was used to load data into Postgre to avoid manually creating tables\n",
    "-\tConnection setup with SQLAlchemy\n",
    "-\tLoop to load multiple CSVs\n",
    "-\tVerification in pgAdmin\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {
    "Snowflake Schema.PNG": {
     "image/png": ""
    }
   },
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0fdef3d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    " ### Schema Design\n",
    "-\tTable relationships:\n",
    "-\torders.Customer ID → customers.Customer ID\n",
    "-\torders.Product Code → products.Product ID\n",
    "-\torders.Port Code → ports.Port Code\n",
    "-\torders.Vessel Code → vessels.Vessel Code\n",
    "-\torders.SR Code → sales_representative.SR Code\n",
    "-   orders.Order Date → dim_date.Date *(Date table created in Power Bi)*\n",
    "-\tcustomers.Customers Segment ID → customers_segment.Segment ID\n",
    "-\tcustomers.Sales Region ID → sales_region.Region ID\n",
    "-\tcustomers.Sales Region ID → sales_region.Region ID\n",
    "-   customers.Customer ID → kpi_customer_revenue.Customer ID\n",
    "-   customers.Customer ID → kpi_above_avg_sales.Customer ID\n",
    "-   customers.Customer ID → kpi_customer_vs_port_zone.Customer ID\n",
    "-\tproducts.Product Category ID → product_category.Product Category ID\n",
    "-\tports.Zone ID → port_zone.Zone ID\n",
    "-\tports.port country code → country_code.Port Country Code\n",
    "-   dim_date.Year → Sales_Target.Year *(Target table created in Power BI)*\n",
    "-   dim_date.YearMonth → kpi_monthly_revenue_analysis.month \n",
    "![Snowflake Schema.PNG](<attachment:Snowflake Schema.PNG>)"
   ]
